WEBVTT

00:00:29.621 --> 00:00:31.039
Good news, everyone.

00:00:31.123 --> 00:00:33.959
I've taught the toaster to feel love.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:43.385
And Hermes returns
from his vacation today.

00:00:43.468 --> 00:00:44.928
Good morning, people.

00:00:45.012 --> 00:00:46.388
Hey, Hermes. Good to see you.

00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:47.723
Yo. My man.

00:00:47.806 --> 00:00:49.850
So, how was the Spleef Nebula?

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:52.269
The flight had a stopover
on the brain slug planet.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.355
Hermes liked it so much,
he decided to stay of his own free will.

00:00:55.439 --> 00:00:56.607
Hermes has all the fun.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.776
Wait a second!
He's got a brain slug on his head.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.987
Shh!
You're going to get us all assimilated.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.656
Just act normal
and switch to a garlic shampoo.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:05.741
On to new business.

00:01:05.824 --> 00:01:08.493
Today's mission is for you all to go
to the brain slug planet.

00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:10.454
What are we going to do there?

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.289
Just walk around, not wearing a helmet.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.666
Sounds great, Hermes!

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.044
Whatever you say.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:19.588
What... Hey, let's ditch him
and go to the movies.

00:01:19.671 --> 00:01:22.174
Hey, yeah, that's a good idea.

00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:24.843
I'm seeing a movie with friends.

00:01:34.228 --> 00:01:35.354
Cool! Let's see this one.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.316
Nah, I'm not in the mood
for a historical documentary.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.861
I've heard good things
about Quizblorg, Quizblorg.

00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:44.488
Ugh, I hate subtitles.

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.698
Alien films are so pretentious.

00:01:46.782 --> 00:01:50.118
Fellows, fellows,
how about a film we can all enjoy?

00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:52.246
Planet of the Clams.

00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:56.208
It's about an upside-down world
where lobster is slave to clam.

00:01:56.291 --> 00:01:57.542
Who invited you?

00:01:57.626 --> 00:01:59.753
The Movie.

00:02:01.463 --> 00:02:03.090
Good point, Bender.

00:02:03.173 --> 00:02:04.549
I'll take a small Slurm.

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:07.678
For only 25 cents less,
you can get a super-small.

00:02:07.761 --> 00:02:08.762
Uh, okay.

00:02:15.102 --> 00:02:16.270
Oh, man!

00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:21.441
Hey, give me a large diet malt liquor
and a popcorn with extra motor oil.

00:02:24.528 --> 00:02:25.988
Down in front!

00:02:33.662 --> 00:02:36.248
Ohh, this is real futuristic.

00:02:36.373 --> 00:02:38.750
Shh! Don't talk during the movie.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.713
New New York Mayor C. Randall Poopenmeyer

00:02:42.796 --> 00:02:45.966
opens a new tube line
to alleviate rush hour traffic.

00:02:49.303 --> 00:02:51.555
Paramecium homeworld.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.974
Newly crowned Miss Universe, Gladys Lennox

00:02:54.057 --> 00:02:57.352
entertains troops fighting
to wipe out the human race.

00:02:57.436 --> 00:02:59.438
Go get 'em, boys!

00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:02.024
And in the world
of Ultimate Robot Fighting,

00:03:02.107 --> 00:03:04.902
the Masked Unit wins his championship bout

00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:08.488
against Gorgeous Gonks
by technical melting.

00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:11.867
Go, Masked Unit!

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:15.245
Uh... Hey, buddy. Yo!

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:16.955
You mind taking your head off?

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:18.123
I'm sorry, sir,

00:03:18.206 --> 00:03:20.083
but I need it to watch the movie.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.920
Just ask flabby over here
to describe it to you, later.

00:03:23.003 --> 00:03:25.672
Sir, she is as the factory made her.

00:03:25.756 --> 00:03:29.426
Well, they should have stopped making her
about halfway through.

00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:48.445
Written by WRITING UNIT 5
and WRITING UNIT 12 &amp; JOE ESZTERHAS

00:03:58.205 --> 00:04:01.041
Well, that finishes this paperwork.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.169
Calculon Enterprises.

00:04:04.253 --> 00:04:08.048
Calculon, a fight scene has broken out
at the special effects warehouse.

00:04:08.131 --> 00:04:09.132
Come, quickly

00:04:09.216 --> 00:04:11.927
before a fiery explosion
chases someone down a hallway.

00:04:14.263 --> 00:04:16.557
I have no choice but to...

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.891
If you want Calculon

00:04:17.975 --> 00:04:22.145
to race to the lasergun battle
in his hover Ferrari, press one.

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:25.941
If you want Calculon
to double-check his paperwork, press two.

00:04:26.024 --> 00:04:27.025
Enter now.

00:04:28.694 --> 00:04:31.154
- You have pressed two.
- No, I didn't.

00:04:31.238 --> 00:04:33.407
I'm almost positive you did.

00:04:35.492 --> 00:04:40.372
Add in the carryover from Form 16-A,
then deduct line 2-B.

00:04:45.168 --> 00:04:46.169
Pardon me, sir,

00:04:46.253 --> 00:04:48.589
but you seem to be
inadvertently kicking my seat.

00:04:48.672 --> 00:04:50.882
Pardon me, sir...

00:04:52.843 --> 00:04:55.095
Yes, that's the gist of what I said.

00:04:55.178 --> 00:04:56.263
Would you mind?

00:04:57.097 --> 00:04:58.098
Sure thing, pal.

00:05:02.978 --> 00:05:05.731
- Sir...
- Who threw that?

00:05:05.814 --> 00:05:06.940
That's it!

00:05:07.024 --> 00:05:11.612
Sir, I challenge you to fisticuffs.

00:05:14.156 --> 00:05:15.198
I'm boned.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.247
Let's all go to the lobby.

00:05:29.838 --> 00:05:33.008
I'm going to open a file
of whoop-ass on you!

00:05:41.308 --> 00:05:43.977
Bender, do you know who that was?

00:05:46.688 --> 00:05:48.941
Cripes! The Masked Unit!

00:05:49.024 --> 00:05:50.859
You knocked him out cold.

00:05:50.984 --> 00:05:53.403
I'm impressed.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.533
Son, I'm the commissioner
of Ultimate Robot Fighting.

00:05:58.617 --> 00:06:01.578
I'm a connoisseur of jerks who pick fights
in movie theaters

00:06:01.662 --> 00:06:03.580
and you're the biggest I've ever seen.

00:06:03.664 --> 00:06:05.165
You should see me at funerals.

00:06:05.249 --> 00:06:08.293
Kid, I want you
in the Ultimate Robot Fighting League.

00:06:08.377 --> 00:06:10.212
Ultimate robot fighting?

00:06:10.295 --> 00:06:12.172
Sounds pleasant. I'll do it.

00:06:14.341 --> 00:06:16.677
My hero. Mwah!

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:21.014
Aw, they don't make movies
like this anymore.

00:06:26.645 --> 00:06:30.107
I'm going to be the greatest
ultimate robot fighter ever.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:33.652
Float like a float-bot,
sting like an automatic stinging machine.

00:06:33.735 --> 00:06:36.446
Bender, you can't be
an ultimate robot fighter.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.449
It's the most brutal form
of competition in the galaxy.

00:06:39.533 --> 00:06:41.660
- It is?
- There are no rules.

00:06:41.743 --> 00:06:44.329
Two robots enter. One robot leaves.

00:06:44.413 --> 00:06:47.874
Then, later, the other robot leaves
after being declared the winner.

00:06:47.958 --> 00:06:49.793
That doesn't sound so bad.

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:52.921
Oh, did I mention the crippling,
agonizing pain?

00:06:53.005 --> 00:06:54.464
I'm pretty sure I did.

00:06:54.548 --> 00:06:55.841
Yes, definitely.

00:06:55.924 --> 00:06:59.428
Crippling pain?
That's not covered by my insurance fraud.

00:06:59.511 --> 00:07:00.804
Count me out.

00:07:00.888 --> 00:07:02.431
No, you've got to do it.

00:07:02.514 --> 00:07:04.391
I don't care how suicidal it is.

00:07:04.474 --> 00:07:05.976
Hey, how come when I want

00:07:06.059 --> 00:07:08.645
to do fun stuff that will kill me,
you're against it?

00:07:08.729 --> 00:07:11.565
This is more important than that
marble-eating contest, Fry.

00:07:11.648 --> 00:07:12.941
It's about pride.

00:07:13.025 --> 00:07:15.027
Let me tell you a story from my childhood.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:17.779
Ugh, again with the orphanarium.

00:07:17.863 --> 00:07:21.366
When I was growing up at the orphanarium,
I got picked on a lot.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.119
My only outlet was octouran kung fu.

00:07:24.703 --> 00:07:26.747
Hi-ya!

00:07:30.042 --> 00:07:31.418
Excellent.

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:34.087
Bill, Keith, you will go
to junior championships.

00:07:34.171 --> 00:07:37.215
Bill, congratulate Keith
when he regains consciousness.

00:07:37.299 --> 00:07:40.802
But Master Funog, I can beat
these dorks with one eye closed.

00:07:40.886 --> 00:07:44.389
Perhaps, but there is more to winning
than beating your opponent.

00:07:44.473 --> 00:07:45.891
You lack the will of a warrior.

00:07:45.974 --> 00:07:48.101
What do you mean? Watch this.

00:07:48.185 --> 00:07:50.896
- Hi-ya!
- Ow!

00:07:50.979 --> 00:07:53.941
No girl has the will of a warrior.

00:07:54.024 --> 00:07:57.402
You have the will of a housewife
or at best, the schoolmarm.

00:07:57.486 --> 00:08:00.280
That's it. I'll take you on right now.

00:08:00.364 --> 00:08:03.559
Very well, but you see,
I have the will of the warrior.

00:08:03.798 --> 00:08:06.092
Therefore, the battle is already over.

00:08:06.136 --> 00:08:07.387
The winner? Me. Ha-ha!

00:08:07.471 --> 00:08:08.972
Rematch? You lose again.

00:08:09.056 --> 00:08:10.641
Had enough? I thought so.

00:08:15.521 --> 00:08:17.523
I lost my chance to be a champion.

00:08:17.606 --> 00:08:19.441
I won't let you throw away yours.

00:08:19.525 --> 00:08:20.776
Leela is right.

00:08:20.859 --> 00:08:22.569
I don't want to end up a loser like her.

00:08:22.653 --> 00:08:24.738
Count me back in.

00:08:24.822 --> 00:08:27.199
Let's see what you got. Touch your toes.

00:08:33.163 --> 00:08:35.874
Still... Can't... Reach.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.501
Hi-ya!

00:08:38.544 --> 00:08:40.879
Hi-ya!

00:08:50.639 --> 00:08:56.812
Let's commence preparations for rumbling!

00:09:03.944 --> 00:09:09.867
Ladies and gentlemen and Smizmars,
welcome to tonight's main event.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.454
In this corner,
from Mom's Friendly Robot factory.

00:09:13.537 --> 00:09:19.001
In America's heartland, Mexico... Bender!

00:09:23.547 --> 00:09:29.762
And in this corner,
from and made of parts unknown,

00:09:29.845 --> 00:09:32.264
the Clear-Cutter.

00:09:36.602 --> 00:09:37.978
Bender rules!

00:09:38.061 --> 00:09:40.397
I got you an official Bender hat.

00:09:40.481 --> 00:09:42.054
Wow! Thanks, Hermes.

00:09:42.079 --> 00:09:44.026
I... Hey, cut that out!

00:09:45.486 --> 00:09:48.238
You can't hit what you can't see.

00:09:54.561 --> 00:09:56.271
Get up, Bender.

00:09:56.355 --> 00:09:59.191
You can't quit
every time you get an ax in the back.

00:10:00.984 --> 00:10:02.986
Or a drill through your face.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.989
Now, quit scratching
your ax hole and get out there.

00:10:15.082 --> 00:10:16.291
Ow, ow.

00:10:20.254 --> 00:10:21.255
Huh?

00:10:22.756 --> 00:10:25.008
And the winner is...

00:10:25.092 --> 00:10:29.846
Bender!

00:10:34.059 --> 00:10:35.394
Nice work out there, kid.

00:10:35.477 --> 00:10:37.938
You know, I think he might be dead.

00:10:38.021 --> 00:10:40.649
I took a life!

00:10:40.732 --> 00:10:42.693
Hi, boss. Yo, dude.

00:10:42.776 --> 00:10:45.070
Hey! He's not dead. What's up with that?

00:10:45.153 --> 00:10:46.780
What, you didn't read the pamphlet?

00:10:46.863 --> 00:10:49.199
Ultimate robot fighting's
a scam, kid. It's rigged.

00:10:50.492 --> 00:10:52.160
It's a secret,
so keep it under your head...

00:10:52.286 --> 00:10:54.913
But the most popular robot always wins.

00:10:54.997 --> 00:10:56.832
You mean I'm not a great fighter?

00:10:56.915 --> 00:11:00.002
- I just won 'cause I'm popular?
- Bingo.

00:11:00.085 --> 00:11:01.878
Woo-hoo! I'm popular!

00:11:01.962 --> 00:11:03.630
In fact, you're more than popular.

00:11:03.714 --> 00:11:05.424
You're pure lowest common denominator.

00:11:05.507 --> 00:11:08.635
Go, Bender. Go, Bender. Go, Bender.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:18.103
Presenting... Bender The Offender.

00:11:18.186 --> 00:11:22.858
I'm just an ex-con trying to go straight
and get my kids back.

00:11:24.693 --> 00:11:25.777
I love you, Bender!

00:11:25.861 --> 00:11:29.781
Versus Billionaire-bot!

00:11:43.128 --> 00:11:45.839
Versus The Foreigner.

00:11:45.923 --> 00:11:52.846
I'm not from here. I have my own customs.
Look at my crazy passport.

00:12:00.938 --> 00:12:05.692
Versus The Chain Smoker.

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:10.530
I love smoking, and after I win the fight,

00:12:10.614 --> 00:12:14.117
I'm headed straight
to your favorite restaurant.

00:12:28.048 --> 00:12:31.552
You know,
I'm also an ultimate robot lover.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.222
Bender, you're three hours late.

00:12:35.305 --> 00:12:38.600
You can't give up on your training now
after both of us worked so hard.

00:12:38.684 --> 00:12:39.893
What do you mean, "we"?

00:12:39.977 --> 00:12:41.103
I said "us."

00:12:41.186 --> 00:12:43.522
Hey, Bender The Offender doesn't need you.

00:12:43.605 --> 00:12:46.149
Bender The Offender doesn't need anybody.

00:12:46.233 --> 00:12:48.151
What about us, Mr. The Offender?

00:12:48.235 --> 00:12:50.320
Well, obviously, I need floozies.

00:12:50.404 --> 00:12:51.446
Let's roll.

00:12:59.788 --> 00:13:01.373
Howdy, chief.

00:13:01.456 --> 00:13:05.335
For my next bout, what do you say I fight
these two bimbos in some mud?

00:13:05.419 --> 00:13:07.713
Actually, we've decided to
go in a different direction.

00:13:07.796 --> 00:13:09.214
What if I told you

00:13:09.298 --> 00:13:11.758
we wouldn't be fighting
in the conventional sense?

00:13:11.842 --> 00:13:13.427
Bender, your popularity is slipping.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:17.014
Sales of your Bender-brand
French-milled bath soaps are down 20%.

00:13:17.764 --> 00:13:19.892
Those morons.

00:13:19.975 --> 00:13:22.477
I said teaberry, not sandalwood.

00:13:22.561 --> 00:13:23.604
Damn it, Bender,

00:13:23.687 --> 00:13:26.773
if you can't move sandalwood
you don't belong in this league!

00:13:26.857 --> 00:13:29.443
That's why you're going
to lose next week's title match.

00:13:29.526 --> 00:13:31.028
But the crowd loves me.

00:13:31.111 --> 00:13:34.656
Perhaps, but let's see how they feel
about your new persona.

00:13:36.074 --> 00:13:40.329
You'll be the most unpopular robot fighter
since Sergeant Feces Processor.

00:13:40.454 --> 00:13:42.706
Oh, yeah?

00:13:42.789 --> 00:13:44.917
Well, what if I don't let the new guy win?

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:48.045
Then, he'll just have to beat you
the old-fashioned way.

00:13:48.128 --> 00:13:49.129
To death!

00:13:49.212 --> 00:13:50.797
Melissa, send in the new kid.

00:13:54.259 --> 00:13:58.388
I... Am... Destructor!

00:14:00.182 --> 00:14:01.808
See you at the fight.

00:14:03.852 --> 00:14:07.481
So then I said, "See you at the fight,"
And that's the story.

00:14:07.564 --> 00:14:10.234
Man, I thought
ultimate robot fighting was real

00:14:10.317 --> 00:14:13.153
like pro wrestling,
but it turns out it's fixed like boxing.

00:14:13.237 --> 00:14:15.864
It's one thing to win a fixed fight.

00:14:15.948 --> 00:14:17.532
There's dignity in that.

00:14:17.616 --> 00:14:19.952
But to lose, and in this atrocity...

00:14:21.203 --> 00:14:22.496
I can't do it.

00:14:22.579 --> 00:14:24.748
Leela, you've got to train me to win.

00:14:24.831 --> 00:14:27.751
No way! If you wouldn't take my help
when you didn't need it,

00:14:27.834 --> 00:14:30.504
why should I give it to you now
when you do need it?

00:14:30.587 --> 00:14:32.756
What the hell are you talking about?

00:14:32.839 --> 00:14:35.425
I don't know, but I'm not helping.

00:14:35.509 --> 00:14:38.512
You loved him as Bender The Offender.

00:14:38.595 --> 00:14:43.100
Now, get ready to hate him
as he threatens your sexuality

00:14:43.183 --> 00:14:47.604
in his new persona, The Gender Bender.

00:14:48.522 --> 00:14:50.899
I'm a real toughie.

00:14:50.983 --> 00:14:55.362
Squaring off this Sunday,
versus... Destructor.

00:14:55.445 --> 00:15:01.285
I will destroy you!

00:15:01.368 --> 00:15:03.453
And stop calling me.

00:15:03.537 --> 00:15:05.914
I am Destructor's trainer, Master Funog.

00:15:05.998 --> 00:15:09.626
My pupil will be victorious
for he has the will of a warrior.

00:15:11.003 --> 00:15:12.588
Not Funog!

00:15:12.671 --> 00:15:14.256
Bender, let's hit the gym.

00:15:14.339 --> 00:15:17.050
I'm going to teach you
to fight like a girl.

00:15:17.134 --> 00:15:20.721
I'll put on my tutu.

00:15:29.104 --> 00:15:33.066
Hello and welcome
to a remarkable championship bout.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:36.194
Destructor, a robotic armored tank

00:15:36.278 --> 00:15:41.074
whose very use in battle
has been ruled a war crime...

00:15:41.158 --> 00:15:46.288
Versus Gender Bender,
who wears a pink tutu.

00:15:46.371 --> 00:15:50.208
This is Rich Little,
imitating Howard Cosell

00:15:50.292 --> 00:15:53.337
here at ringside with George Foreman.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.672
George, a word in edgewise.

00:15:55.756 --> 00:15:59.051
This could be the most
one-sided fight since 1973

00:15:59.134 --> 00:16:02.596
when Ali faced
an 80-foot-tall, mechanical Joe Frazier.

00:16:02.679 --> 00:16:04.514
My memory's not what it used to be,

00:16:04.598 --> 00:16:06.767
but I think
the entire Earth was destroyed.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.894
Interesting, if true.

00:16:08.977 --> 00:16:14.691
The Vegas odds tonight stand
at an unprecedented 1,000:0.

00:16:14.775 --> 00:16:19.988
A bet of zero dollars on Bender
pays $1,000 if he wins.

00:16:20.072 --> 00:16:22.824
Still, very few takers.

00:16:22.908 --> 00:16:24.534
It's not a smart bet.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.161
Hi-ya!

00:16:26.286 --> 00:16:28.038
According to the script,

00:16:28.121 --> 00:16:31.583
you're supposed to prance out
and tickle him with your fairy wand.

00:16:31.667 --> 00:16:34.378
Instead, I want you to prance out
and kick his head off.

00:16:34.461 --> 00:16:36.546
Got it. Large kickle, hold the tickle.

00:16:37.798 --> 00:16:40.801
Thank God, I'm free of that nightmare!

00:16:40.884 --> 00:16:42.553
Sorry, buddy. Here you go.

00:16:42.636 --> 00:16:45.222
Thank you. It was cold
down there on the floor.

00:16:45.305 --> 00:16:47.140
Here, Professor, I got you a program.

00:16:47.224 --> 00:16:51.061
Oh, good.
Just let me put on my reading glasses.

00:16:53.272 --> 00:16:57.442
Why, Zoidberg,
There's a lovely photo of you in here.

00:17:02.281 --> 00:17:07.953
In this corner, the confused young robot
with the golden curls,

00:17:08.036 --> 00:17:11.748
weighing 525 pounds...

00:17:11.832 --> 00:17:16.920
The Gender Bender!

00:17:19.423 --> 00:17:21.717
Get that hippie out of the ring!

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:27.431
And in these two corners,
weighing 400 tons,

00:17:27.514 --> 00:17:32.644
the gizmo from Pismo... Beach.

00:17:32.728 --> 00:17:36.607
Destructor!

00:17:39.318 --> 00:17:42.362
So, we meet again. Most amusing.

00:17:42.446 --> 00:17:45.782
Girl who acts like fighter
training fighter who acts like girl.

00:17:45.866 --> 00:17:47.492
Keep laughing, Funog.

00:17:51.204 --> 00:17:52.456
Ready, Bender?

00:17:52.539 --> 00:17:55.042
I was built ready. Give me the bell.

00:17:55.125 --> 00:17:56.335
Did you hear a noise?

00:18:05.969 --> 00:18:12.684
Final boarding call for Flight 406.
Nonstop service to pain.

00:18:14.728 --> 00:18:16.688
Now boarding stand-by passengers...

00:18:24.238 --> 00:18:27.824
This seems as good a time as any
to bring up my new grill for no reason.

00:18:27.908 --> 00:18:31.578
With its patented design,
the fat drains directly into my mouth.

00:18:39.253 --> 00:18:42.172
Fry, throw in the towel.

00:18:43.924 --> 00:18:47.261
For God sakes, Fry!

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:54.059
That's exactly what I was thinking.

00:18:56.311 --> 00:19:01.984
No!

00:19:02.067 --> 00:19:03.068
Mommy.

00:19:03.151 --> 00:19:05.362
Okay, Funog, that's enough.

00:19:05.445 --> 00:19:06.780
Call him off.

00:19:06.863 --> 00:19:07.906
Funog?

00:19:11.201 --> 00:19:12.202
Hmm.

00:19:15.622 --> 00:19:18.333
Why won't anyone help me?

00:19:25.924 --> 00:19:29.553
- So... Once more, we meet again.
- Huh?

00:19:29.636 --> 00:19:32.764
You didn't train Destructor.
You're just controlling him like a puppet.

00:19:32.848 --> 00:19:36.184
I mean, cheating in a fake fight.
That's low.

00:19:36.268 --> 00:19:38.395
Better than being a girl... Like you.

00:19:38.478 --> 00:19:40.063
You're a girl!

00:19:40.147 --> 00:19:41.565
Oh, right.

00:19:41.648 --> 00:19:43.859
Girls lack the will of the warrior.

00:19:43.984 --> 00:19:45.485
Hi-ya!

00:19:50.908 --> 00:19:53.076
It's Bendering time.

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.453
Take this...

00:19:54.536 --> 00:19:55.662
And this.

00:19:58.248 --> 00:20:00.417
You were an excellent student.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.169
Too bad I was a lousy teacher.

00:20:08.175 --> 00:20:13.013
I think you misunderstood
the concept of Bendering time.

00:20:13.764 --> 00:20:15.766
See you in girl hell.

00:20:15.849 --> 00:20:18.185
I'll be in boy hell, much nicer.

00:20:26.693 --> 00:20:28.695
Yes!

00:20:28.779 --> 00:20:31.031
Yes!

00:20:31.198 --> 00:20:32.199
Ow...

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.620
And the winner is...

00:20:36.703 --> 00:20:38.956
Destructor!

00:20:40.582 --> 00:20:43.877
I've not seen a spectacle of this nature

00:20:43.961 --> 00:20:47.214
in all my years
impersonating a sportscaster.

00:20:47.297 --> 00:20:48.674
It sure was some fight.

00:20:48.757 --> 00:20:50.551
Interesting side note.

00:20:50.634 --> 00:20:53.011
As a head without a body, I envy the dead.

00:20:53.095 --> 00:20:55.013
No argument here.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.185
Bender, how did the fight go?

00:21:00.269 --> 00:21:01.645
I heard somebody got flattened.

00:21:01.728 --> 00:21:03.897
Fry, where's your brain slug?

00:21:05.816 --> 00:21:08.527
Poor little guy starved to death.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.320
I'm proud of you, Bender.

00:21:10.404 --> 00:21:12.281
Sure, you lost, you lost bad,

00:21:12.364 --> 00:21:13.991
but the important thing is

00:21:14.074 --> 00:21:17.995
I beat up someone who hurt
my feelings in high school. Ha-ha!

00:21:18.078 --> 00:21:21.331
I'm in tremendous pain here.

00:21:21.415 --> 00:21:23.000
Great job, kid.

00:21:23.083 --> 00:21:25.919
You lost, and you made it look
almost half-real.

00:21:26.003 --> 00:21:27.754
I want you to have this card

00:21:27.838 --> 00:21:30.257
good for 10 percent off
at Bed, Bath and Beyond.

00:21:32.509 --> 00:21:33.677
Yes...

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:35.387
I'm the greatest...

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:37.681
The greatest!

00:21:38.599 --> 00:21:40.809
And so ends the chronicle

00:21:40.893 --> 00:21:44.521
of one of the greatest
ever to play the sport.

00:21:44.605 --> 00:21:47.024
And he didn't look half-bad in a tutu.

00:21:47.107 --> 00:21:49.943
That he did surely not.

00:21:50.027 --> 00:21:51.028
What?